# Catch it in this session

A hostile review is late. The session that edits a path executes that path before calling the work done. `php -l`, a rendered page, PHPStan, and a test that only checks `method_exists` or a hardcoded string are not a run.

Execute the changed behavior through the same entry the product uses:

- SQL goes through the app's PDO with native prepares. A bare `?` inside `jsonb_build_object` or any other `any` argument is unfinished until the parameter is cast and that statement has run. A job-queue edit includes one `php bin/work.php` pass that finishes.
- An error caught inside a job, then returned as success, never reaches `JobQueue::finish()`. A transport failure must still retry. Only a recipient rejection at `RCPT TO` may mark `email_bounced`. A `535` at login must not.
- A CSV or export edit includes a negative amount and a formula. `-500` stays a number. `=1+1` stays text.
- A money edit includes the abuse case: a release larger than the amount held, a missing booth on the posted lines, a double submit, an actor taken from the form.
- A deploy, route-manifest, or sign-in/lockout edit follows `.cursor/rules/deploy-and-auth-abuse.mdc`: rebuild in the deploy script, spray/distributed lockout vectors, idempotent credential plant.

`maintain-proven-level` and `prove-before-advance` withhold the full `composer check` until this message asks for it. They do not withhold the execution above. A failed run is fixed in this session. If a run cannot be started, name the command and the reason before calling the work done.

```text
BAD: ON CONFLICT added, php -l clean, worker never started
GOOD: enqueue executed; work.php finishes one pass; 535 does not bounce a vendor; -500 stays numeric
```
